hypotheses.statement:
Suppose $a,c\in R$ satisfy $ca=0$. For distinct indices $i,h,j$ and every $b\in R$, $$\label{eq:cut-movement}
 [x_{ij}(ab),x_{ji}(c)]
   =[x_{ih}(a),x_{hi}(bc)].$$ In particular, $[x_{ij}(a),x_{ji}(c)]$ is independent of $j\ne i$. It commutes with both defining roots, has square $1$, and has matrix image $I+acE_{ii}$.

Degree truncations detect the stable Steinberg group: $$\label{eq:stable-detection}
 \bigcap_{d\ge1}
 \ker\bigl(\mathop{\mathrm{St}}(R)\longrightarrow\mathop{\mathrm{St}}(R/R_{\ge d})\bigr)=1.$$

The map $\widetilde S_{r,l}\to S_{r,l}$ is a universal central extension. Consequently the inclusion of the complementary block induces a natural isomorphism $$\label{eq:stabilizer-homology}
 H_2(\mathop{\mathrm{E}}_r(B);\mathbb Z)\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }
 H_2(S_{r,l};\mathbb Z),$$ and both groups identify naturally with $J_r(B)$.

